+Wasmer detects Next.js and builds the site with `yarn build`, which also generates the RSS feed (`public/feed.xml`). No environment variables are required. The button builds this public repository as-is and does not fork it; to make the portfolio your own (`theme.config.js`, `scripts/gen-rss.js`, `pages/posts/*.md`) and redeploy on push, fork the repository and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard.
